## 4. Ollama Interaction

### Ollama Adapter

All Ollama calls go through `app/ollama.py`. This is the single point of contact with Ollama.

### Ollama Functions

| Function | Endpoint | Purpose |
|----------|----------|---------|
| `generate()` | `POST /api/chat` | Non-streaming chat completion |
| `stream()` | `POST /api/chat` (stream) | Streaming chat completion |
| `generate_with_tools()` | `POST /api/chat` | Chat completion with tool definitions |
| `embed()` | `POST /api/embed` | Text embedding |

### Places Ollama Is Called

1. **`_extract_transaction_filters`** (`tools.py:32-39`)
   - Purpose: Extract structured filters from NL query
   - Input: System prompt + user query
   - Expected: JSON with category, type_, start_date, end_date
   - Used by: `search_transactions_nl`

2. **`query_transactions_dynamic`** (`tools.py:281-288`)
   - Purpose: Extract advanced transaction filters
   - Input: System prompt + user query
   - Expected: JSON with merchant, date, amount_min, amount_max, etc.
   - Used by: `transaction_query` intent

3. **`answer_goal_question`** (`assistants.py:82-87`)
   - Purpose: Generate goal planning response
   - Input: System prompt with goal summaries + user question
   - Expected: Natural language response
   - Used by: `goal` agent

4. **`answer_budget_question`** (`assistants.py:167-172`)
   - Purpose: Generate budget analysis
   - Input: System prompt with financial metrics + user question
   - Expected: Natural language response
   - Used by: `budget` agent

5. **`answer_insights_question`** (`insights_agent.py`)
   - Purpose: Generate insights response
   - Input: System prompt with insights data + user question
   - Expected: Natural language response
   - Used by: `insights` agent

6. **`answer_alerts_question`** (`alerts_agent.py`)
   - Purpose: Generate alert analysis
   - Input: System prompt with alerts data + user question
   - Expected: Natural language response
   - Used by: `alert` agent

7. **`explain_chart_or_alert`** (`reports.py`)
   - Purpose: Generate chart/alert explanation
   - Input: System prompt with chart/alert data
   - Expected: Natural language explanation
   - Used by: `chart_alert` agent

8. **`generate_report_narrative`** (`reports.py`)
   - Purpose: Generate narrative summary for report
   - Input: System prompt with report sections
   - Expected: Natural language narrative
   - Used by: `report` agent

9. **`classify_intent`** (via `app/services/intent.py`)
   - Purpose: Classify user intent when no agent specified
   - Input: User message
   - Expected: Intent enum value
   - Used by: Auto-routing in `/chat/agent`

### Ollama Configuration

| Setting | Env Var | Default | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|---------|
| URL | `OLLAMA_URL` | `http://localhost:11434` | Ollama server address |
| Chat Model | `OLLAMA_CHAT_MODEL` | `llama3.2` | Default chat model |
| Embed Model | `OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL` | `nomic-embed-text` | Default embedding model |
| Bypass Mode | `OLLAMA_BYPASS` | `false` | Skip Ollama calls, return synthetic response |
| Temperature | `OLLAMA_TEMPERATURE` | `0.3` | Generation randomness |
| Max Tokens | `OLLAMA_NUM_PREDICT` | `256` | Max tokens to generate |
| Top P | `OLLAMA_TOP_P` | `0.9` | Nucleus sampling |
| Repeat Penalty | `OLLAMA_REPEAT_PENALTY` | `1.1` | Token repetition penalty |

### Ollama Flow Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Agent Handler] --> B{Needs LLM?}
    B -->|Yes| C[build prompt]
    B -->|No| Z[Return data directly]
    C --> D[ollama.generate/stream]
    D --> E{Mode?}
    E -->|Normal| F[HTTP POST /api/chat]
    E -->|Bypass| G[Return synthetic response]
    F --> H{Status 200?}
    H -->|Yes| I[Parse JSON response]
    H -->|No| J[Raise OllamaAdapterError]
    I --> K[Extract message.content]
    K --> L[Return to handler]
    G --> L
    J --> M[Fallback or error message]
```

### Transaction Search Ollama Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[User: Show me Starbucks transactions] --> B[search_transactions_nl]
    B --> C[_extract_transaction_filters]
    C --> D[Ollama generate - filter extraction]
    D --> E{Valid JSON?}
    E -->|Yes| F[Parse filters]
    E -->|No| G[Return empty filters]
    F --> H[GET /api/transactions/ with filters]
    G --> H
    H --> I[Return transaction results]
    I --> J[Route returns: Found X transactions]
```

