## 5. Tool Selection Logic

### Actual Implementation

The backend router selects the agent first. Ollama is never used for agent/tool selection in the current implementation.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[POST /chat/agent] --> B{agent field present?}
    B -->|Yes| C[get_agent lookup in AGENT_REGISTRY]
    B -->|No| D[classify_intent via Ollama]
    C -->|Found| E[Map to Intent enum]
    C -->|Not found| F[400 Unknown agent]
    D --> E
    E --> G[route_intent dispatch]
    G -->|REPORT| H[build_report]
    G -->|CHART_ALERT| I[explain_chart_or_alert]
    G -->|GOAL| J[answer_goal_question]
    G -->|BUDGET| K[answer_budget_question]
    G -->|TRANSACTION_SEARCH| L[search_transactions_nl]
    G -->|INSIGHTS| M[answer_insights_question]
    G -->|DB_CONTEXT| N[answer_database_question]
    G -->|ALERTS| O[answer_alerts_question]
    G -->|TRANSACTION_QUERY| P[query_transactions_dynamic]
    G -->|GENERAL_CHAT| Q[Agent list response]
    G -->|Unknown| R[Fallback message]
```

### Router Implementation

File: `app/services/router.py:58-284`

The `route_intent()` function:
1. Takes `intent: Intent`, `token: str`, `user_id: str`, `message: str`
2. Dispatches to specific handler based on intent
3. Each handler fetches data from Django API
4. Each handler may call Ollama for response generation
5. Returns `{"intent": str, "response": str, "data": Optional[dict], "filters": Optional[dict], "fallback": bool}`

